--TEST--
With no `[log] target`, a `Core\Log::write` inside a request goes to standard error: the response body is only what the program printed, and `Core\Out::capture` around the write captures nothing — `rule:errors/engine-floor` and `rule:security/capture-answers-the-carrier`
--GET--
q=%3Cimg%20src%3Dx%3E
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Log::write
// The query value is markup. A record in the body would put it into the page
// unescaped, beside the source path and the request id it also carries.
var $q = Core\Request::query("q") ?? "";
var $captured = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    Core\Log::write(Core\Log::Level::Warn, "inside a capture", ["q" => $q]);
});
echo "captured [", $captured, "]\n";

Core\Log::write(Core\Log::Level::Warn, "outside a capture", ["q" => $q]);
echo "<p>page</p>\n";
--EXPECT--
captured []
<p>page</p>
